#====================================================================
# E239 — Preserve diagnostics across multi-case Conan consumer tests
#====================================================================

id:                     E239
trigger_tool:           conan|test_package
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        first failing self.run stops remaining consumer cases|non-zero consumer result has no failure output

severity:               2
category:               conan-multi-case-failure-aggregation
match_keywords:         self.run, ConanException, consumer cases, aggregate failures, fail-fast, exit code, test_package
title:                  Preserve complete diagnostics across multi-case Conan test_package runs

root_cause:             Conan self.run raises ConanException on the first non-zero command by default, so a plain loop never executes later independent cases. If the consumer also returns non-zero without printing its case and result, the surviving exception identifies only the command and hides the program-level failure context.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 test_package recipes that invoke one installed-package consumer once per independently named case and need a complete failure inventory from a single test run.
verification_cmd:       Stub two self.run calls to raise distinct ConanException messages, assert every declared case is still called, and verify the final aggregate plus the consumer's non-zero output preserve case names and original results.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           catch-record-continue-then-raise
rec_description:        Catch only ConanException around each self.run call, append the case name and unchanged exception text, continue through the full case list, then raise one ConanException containing every failure. Make the consumer print FAIL plus its case name and result code for recognized non-zero results while returning the same code.
rec_command:            Accumulate f"{case}: {error}" for each ConanException and raise once after the loop; emit "FAIL <case> result=<code>" before returning a recognized non-zero result.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual-conan-test-edit

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      one-ctest-entry-per-case
fallback_description:   Register every case as an independent CTest entry and run CTest with output-on-failure when the target environment and CI contract reliably execute CTest and expose all failures.
fallback_command:       add_test per case and run ctest --output-on-failure
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          cmake-test-registration

forbid_1_pattern:       except\s+Exception
forbid_1_reason:        Catching every exception can hide recipe bugs, configuration errors, and programming defects that are not ordinary command failures.
forbid_1_consequence:   The test may continue after an invalid state and replace the real traceback with a misleading aggregate.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

